<rml>
<head>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="theme.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="context_menu.rcss"/>
</head>
<body data-model="context_menu">
    <!-- Floating right-click context menu (mouse interactivity plan, Step 3).
         FIRST non-fullscreen rml_doc popup in the codebase. #ctx-backdrop is a
         full-viewport transparent click-catcher painted BEHIND the panel (an
         earlier sibling in document order): a click lands on it only when it
         misses the panel, since the panel sits on top and intercepts hits over
         its own rect — the standard web/desktop "click outside to dismiss"
         idiom. Rows are a single flat data-for (this codebase avoids nested
         data-for entirely, see inventory.rml) with both a click and a hover
         handler; keyboard UP/DOWN/CONFIRM in show_context_menu() share the
         same `highlighted` flag as mouse hover, so the row highlight tracks
         either input method identically. -->
    <div id="ctx-backdrop" data-event-click="on_dismiss()"></div>
    <div id="ctx-panel" class="ctx-panel" data-style-left="left_style" data-style-top="top_style">
        <div class="ctx-row" data-for="a : rows"
             data-class-disabled="!a.enabled"
             data-class-selected="a.highlighted"
             data-event-click="on_pick(it_index)"
             data-event-mouseover="on_hover(it_index)">
            <span class="ctx-label" data-rml="a.label_rml"></span>
            <span class="ctx-hotkey" data-rml="a.hotkey_rml"></span>
        </div>
    </div>
</body>
</rml>
